{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYuvBqp4knkHhpeXa8i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI's latest safety update describes a change in what ChatGPT weighs before it answers: the request, plus what earlier conversations and a prediction of the user's age suggest about it. The company says a request that seems ordinary can take on a different meaning in light of an earlier conversation. In May it described how ChatGPT can use short, factual summaries of earlier warning signs in a later chat. It now says it is building on that work, so that when recent chats show warning signs of possible violence, ChatGPT will respond more conservatively when sharing information that could be misused.\n\nAge works the same way. OpenAI says it will apply those stricter limits to users it predicts are under 18, even if their chats show no sign of violent intent. For teens it is also restricting practical information about weapons and security systems, even when a question appears harmless. The prediction comes from the age prediction system launched last year, which estimates from multiple signals, such as behavior patterns, whether someone is under or over 18. OpenAI says it has strengthened the system to keep assessing new signals. Adults placed in the teen experience by mistake can confirm their age through Persona, its age verification partner, in what the company calls a fast, privacy-protective process.\n\nIt follows from this design that two people sending the same question can receive different answers, depending on their recent chat history or the system's estimate of their age. The announcement offers no data on how often adults are misclassified or how often conversations are flagged wrongly, and OpenAI acknowledges it is still working on recognizing warning signs reliably and deciding when and how to intervene. Those rates will determine how much legitimate use these limits get in the way of. The first Community Safety Report, planned for early 2027, is where such figures might appear, though the company has said only that it will include relevant data on how well its safeguards work."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1136,"cache_read_input_tokens":3667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1136},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16675d8d-fb07-4158-9574-927ab2753178","uuid":"d57f7dd8-8a58-4dd9-8c72-c43639c9f610","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:29:55.258Z","request_id":"req_011CgdYuuxwyYNTHdbj8CjD1"}
